Strong Final Interview Answer

A Snowflake Virtual Warehouse is an independent massively parallel processing compute cluster responsible for executing queries and data processing workloads. Warehouses form the compute layer of Snowflake’s architecture and can scale independently without impacting storage. Snowflake warehouses support elastic scaling both vertically and horizontally, enabling optimization for either single-query performance or concurrency. Warehouses can be suspended and resumed instantly, which is important for cost optimization because suspended warehouses consume no credits. Each warehouse also maintains a local SSD cache to improve repeated query performance.
